    "question": "Solve $2\\sin^2\\theta + 5\\cos\\theta - 4 = 0$ for $0^\\circ \\le \\theta < 360^\\circ$. (Separate by comma, smallest first)",
    "question_zh": "解方程 $2\\sin^2\\theta + 5\\cos\\theta - 4 = 0$（$0^\\circ \\le \\theta < 360^\\circ$）。（以逗號分隔，由小到大排列）",
    "answer": "60, 300",
    "correct_answer": "60, 300",
    "solution_steps": [
      "1. Use $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$.",
      "2. $2(1 - \\cos^2\\theta) + 5\\cos\\theta - 4 = 0$.",
      "3. $2 - 2\\cos^2\\theta + 5\\cos\\theta - 4 = 0 \\implies 2\\cos^2\\theta - 5\\cos\\theta + 2 = 0$.",
      "4. $(2\\cos\\theta - 1)(\\cos\\theta - 2) = 0$.",
